From: Justin Walsh <contact.me@thejustinwalsh.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 05:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] CUDA FA vec kernel: skip KV cells every query masks out

With a unified KV cache (llama-server's auto -np: 4 slots, one pool) a
decode step attends over the pool up to its highest used cell
(llama_kv_cache::get_n_kv pads used_max_p1()), and the cells of OTHER
sequences are masked -inf. The vec kernel -- the one decode and
speculative verification use (<= 2 queries on Ada+ with quantized K/V,
<= 8 in batch-invariant mode) -- still reads and multiplies every one
of them: mask_to_KV_max, which trims a masked tail, runs only for
>= 1024 queries or several sequences. Measured on an RTX 5060 Ti
(Bonsai 2 27B, q8_0 K/V, -c 181248): one slot at 8k decodes at 60.6
tok/s alone and 36.7 with another slot's 40k cells below it.

Each warp owns 32 cells of the chunk for both the KQ and the VKQ part,
so a warp whose cells are -inf for every valid query column skips its
body. Masked cells contribute exp(-inf) = 0 to KQ_sum and VKQ and leave
KQ_max unchanged, so the result is bit-identical (and a NaN left in an
empty cell can no longer reach the output through 0 * NaN).
---
 ggml/src/ggml-cuda/fattn-vec.cuh | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+)

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/fattn-vec.cuh b/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/fattn-vec.cuh
index 69dd936..dd51beb 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/fattn-vec.cuh
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/fattn-vec.cuh
@@ -254,6 +254,25 @@ static __global__ void flash_attn_ext_vec(
     for (int k_VKQ_0 = blockIdx.y*nthreads; k_VKQ_0 < k_VKQ_max; k_VKQ_0 += gridDim.y*nthreads,
              // Increment pointers after each loop:
              K += gridDim.y*nthreads*nb11, V += gridDim.y*nthreads*nb21, maskh += gridDim.y*nthreads) {
+        // Skip KV cells that every query of this block masks out. Each warp owns cells
+        // [threadIdx.y*WARP_SIZE, (threadIdx.y + 1)*WARP_SIZE) of this chunk for both the KQ and the VKQ part
+        // (the KQ shared buffer is only read back by the warp that wrote it), so a warp whose 32 cells are all
+        // -inf for every valid column can skip its body: such cells add exp(-inf) = 0 to KQ_sum and VKQ and
+        // leave KQ_max unchanged (scale expf(0) = 1), so the result is the same. With a unified KV cache the
+        // cells of OTHER sequences are masked, and without this each decode step read them all, up to the
+        // highest used cell. The increments in the for statement still run on `continue`.
+        if (mask) {
+            int live = 0;
+#pragma unroll
+            for (int j = 0; j < ncols; ++j) {
+                if (ncols == 1 || ic0 + j < int(ne01.z)) {
+                    live |= __half2float(maskh[j*ne11 + tid]) != -INFINITY;
+                }
+            }
+            if (!warp_reduce_any(live)) {
+                continue;
+            }
+        }
 
         // Calculate KQ tile and keep track of new maximum KQ values:
         float KQ_reg[ncols]; // KQ in registers.
